lox init: /project

Prerequisites
  ok  Docker 29.0.0
  ok  cosign (lox add and lox up verify every image's signature)
  ok  lea
  ok  launchers: locksql, lockmq, lockfile, lockhttp

Detected (read only: .env*, compose*.yaml, config/; no secret is read or kept)
  1  PostgreSQL  host.docker.internal:55432  user shop, database shop, tls disable
       from compose.yaml (service db), .env (DATABASE_URL)
  2  RabbitMQ    http://host.docker.internal:55672  user orders, vhost orders, AMQP amqp://host.docker.internal:55673
       from compose.yaml (service mq)
  3  MySQL       inventory.internal:3307  user stock, database stock, tls verify-full
       from config/inventory.yaml

Plan (nothing is written before your yes)
  locksql db
    locksql profile add --profile db --credentials ask --engine postgres --host host.docker.internal --port 55432 --user shop --database shop --tls disable
    then locksql init claude, locksql doctor --fix, lox add locksql db --profile db
    doctor --fix: it also wires your installed agents for your account
    doctor --fix needs locksql v0.13.1 or later (launcher and image); with an older one, doctor without --fix
    allowed_uids [1000]: lea's agents run as uid 1000
  lockmq mq
    lockmq profile add --profile mq --credentials ask --url http://host.docker.internal:55672 --user orders --vhost orders --amqp-url amqp://host.docker.internal:55673
    then lockmq init claude, lockmq doctor --fix, lox add lockmq mq --profile mq
    doctor --fix needs lockmq v0.6.1 or later (launcher and image); with an older one, doctor without --fix
    allowed_uids [1000]: lea's agents run as uid 1000
  locksql stock
    locksql profile add --profile stock --credentials ask --engine mysql --host inventory.internal --port 3307 --user stock --database stock --tls verify-full
    then locksql init claude, locksql doctor --fix, lox add locksql stock --profile stock
    doctor --fix: it also wires your installed agents for your account
    doctor --fix needs locksql v0.13.1 or later (launcher and image); with an older one, doctor without --fix
    allowed_uids [1000]: lea's agents run as uid 1000
Then lox up shows the whole change for your review: nothing starts without your yes there.

locksql db
  profile add: profile db written to /project/.locksql/config.toml (credentials ask)
  init claude: the agent's files written
  doctor --fix: fixed chmod go-w .locksql/config.toml
  doctor --fix: 1 ok, 2 warning(s), 1 failed (advisory before lox up)
    project: owned by you (chown)
  lox add: lock db declared
lockmq mq
  profile add: profile mq written to /project/.lockmq/config.toml (credentials ask)
  init claude: the agent's files written
  doctor --fix: fixed chmod go-w .lockmq/config.toml
  doctor --fix: 1 ok, 2 warning(s), 1 failed (advisory before lox up)
    project: owned by you (chown)
  lox add: lock mq declared
locksql stock
  profile add: profile stock written to /project/.locksql/config.toml (credentials ask)
  init claude: the agent's files written
  doctor --fix: fixed chmod go-w .locksql/config.toml
  doctor --fix: 1 ok, 2 warning(s), 1 failed (advisory before lox up)
    project: owned by you (chown)
  lox add: lock stock declared

lox up: review the change

Each console that started asks its questions here: its policy (y to approve it, on a first start) and the password it does not read from Vault (masked). Detach with Ctrl-P Ctrl-Q once it says Listening.




Run `lea` (or `claude` + `lox approve`).
